2026-02-21T21:02:03.069870Z TRACE codex_tui::markdown_stream: markdown finalize (raw source):
---
Implementation plan from here:

1. Audit current plugin system and Wiki plugin code paths (`types` → `main runtime/api/ipc` → `preload` → `renderer workbench` → plugin manifest/runtime) to map each of the 26 tasks to concrete files.
2. Implement core host primitives first (type contracts, task runtime, chat bridge, IPC/preload APIs) so downstream Wiki/UI work can use stable interfaces.
3. Implement Wiki scanning/indexing + chat integration and canvas protocol extensions, then update workbench shell to consume protocol-driven task/chat blocks.
4. Add/adjust tests and run targeted checks (`lint`/`typecheck` scope depending on scripts).
5. Mark completed checklist items in `openspec/changes/plugin-wiki-deepwiki-capabilities/tasks.md` as each task lands; pause only if a real blocker appears.

I’m starting step 1 now by reading the core files in that dependency order.

---
